cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, a citation is welcome and is not required (it is CC0)."
title: "segmento_II.py: vanishing weighted sums of completely multiplicative functions, computed"
abstract: >-
  One file, Python 3 standard library only, exact integer arithmetic. Exhibits, for admissible
  lengths m up to 10^6, a completely multiplicative function with values +-1 whose weighted sum
  sum_{n<=m} n eps(n) vanishes, recomputing the sum; re-verifies the 104 interval certificates that
  prove it for 5000 <= m < 10^8; computes the digit set R_q of a Legendre symbol and the zeros it
  propagates, each by direct summation and by the digit recursion; checks the weighted half-sum
  formula on every odd Dirichlet character mod f, exactly in Z[zeta_N]; and lists the cells on
  which Conrey's sine series of the Legendre symbol vanishes identically. Declines, with a message,
  outside the hypotheses of the statements it implements.
